<http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Quantity Value expresses the magnitude and kind of a quantity and is given by the product of a numerical value n and a unit of measure U. The number multiplying the unit is referred to as the numerical value of the quantity expressed in that unit. Refer to \"http://physics.nist.gov/Pubs/SP811/sec07.html\", NIST SP 811, section 7 for more on quantity values." .
