# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The thing whose property is being estimated or calculated in the course of an Observation to arrive at a Result or whose property is being manipulated by an Actuator, or which is being sampled or transformed in an act of Sampling."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Feature Of Interest"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "When measuring the height of a tree, the height is the observed ObservableProperty, 20m may be the Result of the Observation, and the tree is the FeatureOfInterest. A window is a FeatureOfInterest for an automatic window control Actuator."@en .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An observable quality (property, characteristic) of a FeatureOfInterest."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Observable Property"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The height of a tree, the depth of a water body, or the temperature of a surface are examples of observable properties, while the value of a classic car is not (directly) observable but asserted."@en .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Act of carrying out an (Observation) Procedure to estimate or calculate a value of a property of a FeatureOfInterest. Links to a Sensor to describe what made the Observation and how; links to an ObservableProperty to describe what the result is an estimate of, and to a FeatureOfInterest to detail what that property was associated with"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Observation"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The activity of estimating the intensity of an Earthquake using the Mercalli intensity scale is an Observation as is measuring the moment magnitude, i.e., the energy released by said earthquake."@en .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Device, agent (including humans), or software (simulation) involved in, or implementing, a Procedure. Sensors respond to a stimulus, e.g., a change in the environment, or input data composed from the results of prior Observations, and generate a Result. Sensors can be hosted by Platforms."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sensor"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Accelerometers, gyroscopes, barometers, magnetometers, and so forth are Sensors that are typically mounted on a modern smart phone (which acts as Platform). Other examples of sensors include the human eyes."@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An equipment monitors that controls properties of a specific vehicle such as its speed or the access to certain city areas."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Un equipo que controla propiedades de un vehículo específico, como su velocidad o el acceso a ciertas áreas de la ciudad."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Control equipment"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#ControlEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Equipo de control"@es .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Feature> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Incidencia que ocurre en el sistema de tráfico de una ciudad"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Incident in the traffic system of a city"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Incidencia"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Incident"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Incidencia planificada, puede ser recurrente o no"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Planned traffic incident"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Incidencia planificada"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#PlannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Planned incident"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Feature> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Section/s defined by a starting and an ending point that can belong to one or more street."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Tramo definido por un punto de inicio y fin que puede pertenecer a una o más vías"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Street section"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#StreetSection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tramo"@es .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql#Feature> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Equipment that allows measuring vehicle traffic or some property of a specific vehicle such as its speed."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Equipo de tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Equipo que permite medir el tráfico de vehículos o alguna propiedad de un vehículo específico como por ejemplo su velocidad."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Traffic equipment"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficEquipment> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Tipo de dispositivo de tráfico que realiza mediciones de propiedades como el nivel de servicio, la intensidad del tráfico y la carga de tráfico."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Type of traffic device which performs measurementsof properties such as service level, traffic intensity and traffic load."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispositivo de medición de tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficMeasurementDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Traffic measuring device"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Observation> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Observación mediante un dispositivo de medición de tráfico o un equipo de control, como radares de velocidad o sistemas de reconocimiento automático de matrículas (ANPR)."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Observation by a traffic measuring device or a control equipment such as speed cameras or Automatic Number Plate Recognition (ANPR) systems."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Observación del tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Traffic observation"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/FeatureOfInterest> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Points where traffic or specific vehicle observations can be made using sensors."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Puntos en donde se pueden realizar observaciones de tráfico o de vehículos específicos."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Punto de observación de tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficObservationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Traffic observation point"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservableProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Generalización de las propiedades observables de medición de tráfico y las propiedades observables de control de vehículos específicos."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Generalization of the observable properties of traffic measurement and the observable properties of control of specific vehicles."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Propiedad de tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Traffic property"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#Incident> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Incidencia no planificada del tráfico de una ciudad"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Unplanned traffic incident"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Incidencia no planificada"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#UnplannedIncident> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unplanned incident"@en .
# 
# 
# 
# #################################################################
# #
# #    Individuals
# #
# #################################################################
# 
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It is obtained by the equation of intensity and time of occupation with certain correction factors. It is expressed as a percentage: a 100% load implies circulatory collapse, interrupted circulation, while 0% implies empty street. It is similar to the Level of Service of the road that is usually measured with the letters A, B, C, D, E and F: level A, between 0% and 20% load; level F, between 90% and 100% load. The level of service is complex to measure and that is why the load is used."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Se refiere al tipo de vehículos que se suman en la intensidad y a día de hoy sólo se pueden medir a mano mediante muestreo y calcular coeficientes de corrección para las intensidad. Los vehículos se deben referir a vehículos tipo y estiman valores aproximados: turismo=1 ; motocicleta=0,75; Bicicleta=0,5; Autobús=1,5; Camión grande=2."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "composicion"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#composition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "composition"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#density
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Property that points out the number of vehicles  occupying a section of roadway (highway, carriageway, or lane) per unit of length at a given moment. It is a key congestion indicator that reduces speed."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Propiedad que indica el número de vehículos que ocupan un tramo de vía (carretera, calzada o carril) por unidad de longitud en un instante determinado. Es un indicador clave de congestión que disminuye la velocidad y la libertad de maniobra."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "densidad de tráfico"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#density> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "traffic density"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Intensidad o aforo, número de vehículos en unidad de tiempo (hora, día, mes año). Los habituales son hora y día."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Intensity or capacity, number of vehicles in time unit (hour, day, month, year). The usual ones are hour and day."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "intensidad"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#intensity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "traffic intensity"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#level
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Calculado a partir de la velocidad, requiere una ecuación o unos niveles de velocidad asociados: verde, fluido; amarillo, lento; naranja, denso; rojo, congestión; negro, circulación interrumpida; gris, sin datos"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Calculated from the speed, it requires an equation or associated speed levels: green, fluid; yellow, slow; orange, dense; red, congestion; black, traffic interrupted; grey, no data."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "level"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#level> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "nivel"@es .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#load
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It is obtained by the equation of intensity and time of occupation with certain correction factors. It is expressed as a percentage: a 100% load implies circulatory collapse, interrupted circulation, while 0% implies empty street. It is similar to the Level of Service of the road that is usually measured with the letters A, B, C, D, E and F: level A, between 0% and 20% load; level F, between 90% and 100% load. The level of service is complex to measure and that is why the load is used."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Se obtiene mediante ecuación de intensidad y tiempo de ocupación con ciertos factores de corrección. Se expresa en tanto por ciento: una carga del 100% implica colapso circulatorio, circulación interrumpida, mientras que 0% implica calle vacía. Es similar al Nivel de Servicio de la vía que habitualmente se mide con las letras A, B, C, D, E y F: nivel A, entre 0% y 20% de carga; nivel F, entre 90% y 100% de carga. El nivel de servicio es complejo de medir y por eso se usa la carga."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "carga"@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#load> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "traffic load"@en .
# 
# https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://edint.es/def/trafico#TrafficProperty> .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Es la ocupación del detector mientras está pasando por encima un vehículo, está asociado a detectores tipo espira electromagnética, y es el tiempo desde que el detector detecta al vehículo hasta que deja detectarlo."@es .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "It is the occupation of the detector while it is passing over a vehicle, it is associated with electromagnetic loop type detectors, and it is the time from when the detector detects the vehicle until it allows it to be detected."@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "occupation"@en .
<https://edint.es/def/trafico#occupation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ocupación"@es .
